"""29 October 2026 : ZenRay Lines JUNCTIONS, the surface between tubes closed by bridges, cut like the pattern of a garment.
EN: the open ends of the tubes (the neck, the shoulders and the hips of a body ; the wrist and the digits of a hand) are holes of a sphere. Bridges join the corners of the open rings to a few POLE nodes
and to each other, so that every face of the network is a patch of 3 to 6 sides that the engine can mesh.
  - BODY (torso) : a front centre line and a back centre line run in the plane of symmetry from the front of the neck to the crotch, with two poles on each (chest F1/B1, belly F2/B2) ; the chest pole
    is joined to the neck and to both armholes, the belly pole to both legs ; the shoulder seams join neck and arms, the side seams join arms and legs, the crotch seam joins the legs. 5 holes give 10
    faces : 3 pentagons and 2 hexagons per side.
  - every bridge is the shortest path on the surface (restricted to the trunk side of the holes), smoothed into a clean curve by a flow that is projected back on the surface ; one half is built and
    MIRRORED for the other (exact symmetry), a curve on the plane of symmetry is projected onto that plane, a curve that crosses it is symmetrized.
  - HAND : the same smoothed bridges around two poles (palm and back), no mirror.
    python -I ZrlJunction.py doc.json --out doc2.json
FR : jonctions coupées comme un patron de vêtement : ligne centrale dans le plan de symétrie, coutures d'épaule et de côté, miroir exact gauche droite, courbes lissées sur la surface.
"""
